{% extends "layout/gates.twig" %}

{#
  ONE ANSWER, ON ITS OWN PAGE.

  ── WHAT THE SECOND PASS ADDED, AND WHY EACH ONE EARNS ITS SPACE ────────────

  READING PROGRESS   A hairline at the very top. On a phone the article is four
                     or five screens and there is no other signal of how much is
                     left — and "how much more of this is there" is exactly the
                     question somebody asks before giving up and opening a ticket.

  READ TIME          "1 min read" beside the category. Same job, before the scroll
                     rather than during it.

  COPY LINK          Because pasting an answer into a reply is a STATED workflow
                     for this team — it is half the reason articles got URLs at
                     all — and asking support staff to select a browser address
                     bar on a phone is not a workflow, it is an obstacle.

  PREV / NEXT        The rail used to offer "All answers" and "Contact a person":
                     a dead end dressed as navigation. Somebody who has just read
                     about a missing payment very often wants the next payment
                     answer, and had to go back to the index and start again.

  SIBLING LIST       The real contents of this category, with the current one
                     marked, so the reader can see where they are rather than
                     just what else exists.

  HIGHLIGHT TO ASK   Select any sentence and a button appears at the selection,
                     carrying that exact text into the assistant. A general
                     article answers the general case; the moment somebody doubts
                     it is always a SPECIFIC sentence. Their only route was to
                     scroll to the bottom, open the assistant, and retype the bit
                     they were unsure about from memory. Most people just left.

                     grab() guards four ways, each one earning its place, and
                     three of them are here because Chromium found the bug:

                     1. NON-TRIVIAL. A stray tap selects one word, and a single
                        word is not a question. Twelve characters minimum.

                     2. BOTH ENDS INSIDE THE ANSWER. It used to test only the
                        anchor — the end the drag STARTED at. So a fast drag that
                        began in a paragraph and overshot past the end of the
                        article was accepted, and the button then offered to ask
                        about a passage whose tail was site furniture. Reproduced
                        with a real mouse drag: the quoted text came back as
                        "Nominations open — 2026 Cycle · live in …", which is the
                        announcement bar. Anchor AND focus are checked now.

                     3. ON SCREEN. The pill sat at r.top - 10 with no clamp, so a
                        selection whose rect began above the fold put it at
                        top:-95 — rendered, unclickable, and pointing at nothing.
                        place() clamps into the viewport and flips the pill BELOW
                        the selection when there is no room above it.

                     4. STILL VISIBLE. It is fixed-positioned while the article
                        scrolls underneath, and the position was computed once, so
                        scrolling left the pill behind pointing at whatever text
                        had moved into its place. place() re-runs on scroll and
                        resize, and drops the pill once the selection leaves the
                        viewport.

                     Capped at 240 characters — the assistant gets a question, not
                     a pasted essay. It follows the SELECTION rather than the
                     pointer, so it works from a keyboard and from a touch
                     long-press.

                     NOTE FOR ANYONE EDITING THE x-data BELOW: it is an HTML
                     attribute delimited by double quotes. A double quote anywhere
                     inside it — including inside a comment — terminates the
                     attribute and silently breaks the ENTIRE component, taking
                     copy-link and the progress bar down with it. That is exactly
                     how this shipped broken the first time. Keep prose up here.

  NOT A STICKY ASK BAR. Tried, measured, removed. The site already pins a bottom
  nav AND a floating assistant button on mobile; a third fixed element rendered
  behind the nav entirely, and stacking three of them over a 390px screen costs
  more reading area than the shortcut was worth. The FAB already carries that job.

  The measure stays ~62 characters and the rail still collapses BELOW the answer,
  never above it: on a phone the rail is not context, it is an obstacle between a
  worried person and the first sentence.
#}

{% block head_styles %}
<style nonce="{{ csp_nonce }}">
  /* The same paper as the Help Centre index and the topic pages. This page was on
     #eef0ec while those two moved to #f0f2f2, and a section whose ground shifts as you
     click through it reads as three sites rather than one. */
  body[data-page="help"]{ background:#f0f2f2; color:var(--ag-ink); }
  .ha{ max-width:1020px; margin:0 auto; padding:clamp(1.2rem,4vw,2.1rem) var(--ag-gutter,32px) clamp(3rem,6vw,4rem); }

  /* Reading progress. Fixed, hairline, above everything but the site header. */
  .ha-prog{ position:fixed; inset:0 auto auto 0; width:100%; height:3px; z-index:60; background:transparent; pointer-events:none; }
  .ha-prog__b{ height:100%; width:0; background:linear-gradient(90deg,#7FC87C,#177015); transition:width .08s linear; }

  .ha-crumb{ display:flex; align-items:center; gap:7px; font-size:12.5px; color:var(--ag-ink-soft); margin-bottom:16px; flex-wrap:wrap; }
  /* Standalone navigation rather than a link in a sentence, so it does not get SC
     2.5.8's inline exception — it measured 19.4px tall. */
  .ha-crumb a{ display:inline-flex; align-items:center; min-height:24px;
    color:var(--ag-ink-soft); text-decoration:none; }
  .ha-crumb a:hover{ color:var(--ag-green); }
  .ha-crumb svg{ flex:none; opacity:.5 }

  .ha-grid{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) 272px; gap:30px; align-items:start; }
  /* The article and its prev/next are ONE column. Left as a sibling of the grid,
     the strip spanned the full page and its "Next" card sat under the rail —
     visually attached to the sidebar rather than to the answer it follows. */
  .ha-col{ min-width:0; }
  .ha-main{ background:var(--ag-surface); border:1px solid rgba(16,41,44,.10); border-radius:14px; padding:clamp(1.4rem,3.5vw,2.4rem); }

  /* head */
  .ha-meta{ display:flex; align-items:center; gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap; }
  /* A mono kicker, not a tinted pill. The pill took the topic's own colour, which put
     a pink chip at the top of a payments answer for no reason a reader could act on —
     the topic is a label here, not a status. Same micro-label as every other surface. */
  .ha-tag{ display:inline-block; font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace); font-size:10.5px;
    font-weight:700; letter-spacing:.22em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#745001; }
  .ha-read{ font-size:12px; color:#5a6d6f; }
  .ha-copy{ margin-left:auto; cursor:pointer; font-family:inherit; font-size:12px; font-weight:600; display:inline-flex;
    align-items:center; gap:6px; padding:7px 12px; border-radius:999px; border:1px solid rgba(16,41,44,.14);
    background:var(--ag-surface); color:#4a5256; }
  .ha-copy:hover{ border-color:var(--ag-green); color:var(--ag-green-dark,#177015); }
  .ha-copy.is-done{ border-color:#bfe0bd; background:#eef7ee; color:#1a6118; }

  .ha-main h1{ margin:14px 0 0; font-family:var(--ag-font-display); font-weight:700; font-size:clamp(1.45rem,3.4vw,2rem); line-height:1.2; letter-spacing:-.015em; }
  .ha-sum{ margin:12px 0 0; font-size:16.5px; line-height:1.6; color:#39464a; font-weight:500; max-width:62ch; }
  .ha-rule{ border:none; border-top:1px solid rgba(16,41,44,.09); margin:22px 0; }

  /* prose */
  .ha-body{ max-width:62ch; }
  .ha-body p{ margin:0 0 16px; font-size:15.5px; line-height:1.72; color:#39464a; }
  .ha-body p:last-child{ margin-bottom:0; }
  .ha-body a{ color:var(--ag-green-dark,#177015); text-decoration:underline; text-underline-offset:2px; }
  .ha-body strong{ color:var(--ag-ink); font-weight:650; }
  .ha-body code{ font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:.88em; background:#eef2ef;
    border:1px solid rgba(16,41,44,.09); border-radius:5px; padding:1px 5px; white-space:nowrap; }

  /* Own counter so the number survives a line wrap without the text sliding
     underneath it — which is what the default list marker does. */
  .ha-steps{ counter-reset:s; list-style:none; margin:0 0 18px; padding:0; }
  .ha-steps li{ counter-increment:s; position:relative; padding:0 0 0 40px; margin-bottom:14px; font-size:15.5px; line-height:1.65; color:#39464a; }
  .ha-steps li:last-child{ margin-bottom:0; }
  .ha-steps li::before{ content:counter(s); position:absolute; left:0; top:1px; width:26px; height:26px; border-radius:50%;
    background:#eef7ee; color:#1a6118; font-size:13px; font-weight:700; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; }

  .ha-note{ display:flex; gap:11px; background:#f4f7f4; border:1px solid #d6e8d3; border-radius:14px;
    padding:15px 17px; margin:0 0 16px; font-size:14.5px; line-height:1.62; color:#2d4a2c; }
  .ha-note svg{ flex:none; margin-top:2px }
  .ha-note a{ color:#177015 }

  /* ── HIGHLIGHT TO ASK ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Select any sentence in the answer and a small button appears at the
     selection, carrying that exact text into the assistant.

     Why: a general article answers the general case, and the moment somebody
     doubts it is a specific sentence — "up to 6 hours late", "one per category".
     Their only route was to scroll to the bottom, open the assistant, and retype
     the bit they were unsure about from memory. Most people just leave.

     The button follows the SELECTION, not the pointer, so it works from a
     keyboard and from a touch long-press. It is fixed-positioned because the
     article scrolls under it and an absolutely-positioned one drifts. */
  .ha-sel{ position:fixed; z-index:70; transform:translate(-50%,-100%); }
  /* Set by place() when the selection is too close to the top of the viewport to
     hang the pill above it — otherwise it renders off-screen and unclickable. */
  .ha-sel.is-below{ transform:translate(-50%,0); }
  .ha-sel button{ cursor:pointer; border:none; font-family:inherit; font-weight:650; font-size:12.5px;
    padding:9px 15px; border-radius:999px; background:#10292C; color:#fff; white-space:nowrap;
    box-shadow:0 8px 22px -8px rgba(16,41,44,.6); display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:7px; }
  .ha-sel button:hover{ background:#177015 }
  /* A visible tint on the selection itself, so it is obvious WHAT the button
     will carry — the browser default is easy to lose against a light card. */
  .ha-body ::selection, .ha-sum::selection{ background:#cfeccd; color:#10292C; }

  /* did this help */
  .ha-fb{ margin-top:26px; padding-top:22px; border-top:1px solid rgba(16,41,44,.09); }
  .ha-fb__q{ font-size:14px; font-weight:600; color:var(--ag-ink); }
  .ha-fb__r{ display:flex; gap:9px; margin-top:12px; flex-wrap:wrap; }
  .ha-fb__b{ cursor:pointer; font-family:inherit; font-size:13.5px; font-weight:600; padding:10px 18px; border-radius:999px;
    border:1px solid rgba(16,41,44,.16); background:var(--ag-surface); color:#39464a; text-decoration:none; display:inline-block; }
  .ha-fb__b:hover{ border-color:var(--ag-green); color:var(--ag-green-dark,#177015); }
  .ha-fb__ok{ font-size:14px; color:#1a6118; font-weight:600; }

  /* prev / next */
  .ha-pn{ display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:12px; margin-top:18px; }
  .ha-pn a{ display:block; background:var(--ag-surface); border:1px solid rgba(16,41,44,.08); border-radius:16px;
    padding:14px 16px; text-decoration:none; transition:border-color .15s; }
  .ha-pn a:hover{ border-color:var(--ag-green); }
  .ha-pn__l{ display:block; font:600 10.5px/1 var(--ag-font-body); letter-spacing:.09em; text-transform:uppercase; color:#5a6d6f; }
  .ha-pn__t{ display:block; margin-top:6px; font-size:14px; font-weight:600; line-height:1.4; color:var(--ag-ink); }
  .ha-pn__next{ text-align:right; }
  /* When there is no previous, the next must not slide left into its place. */
  .ha-pn__gap{ display:block }

  /* rail */
  .ha-side{ display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:14px; position:sticky; top:88px; }
  .ha-box{ background:var(--ag-surface); border:1px solid rgba(16,41,44,.10); border-radius:14px; padding:18px 20px; }
  .ha-box h2{ margin:0 0 12px; font-family:var(--ag-font-mono,monospace); font-size:10.5px;
    font-weight:700; line-height:1.4; letter-spacing:.22em; text-transform:uppercase;
    color:#626a6e; }
  .ha-box ul{ list-style:none; margin:0; padding:0; }
  .ha-box li + li{ border-top:1px solid rgba(16,41,44,.06); }
  .ha-box a{ display:block; padding:9px 0; font-size:13.5px; line-height:1.5; color:#39464a; text-decoration:none; }
  .ha-box a:hover{ color:var(--ag-green); }
  .ha-box a[aria-current]{ color:var(--ag-green-dark,#177015); font-weight:650; }

  /* Flat. The radial-gradient orb that used to sit in this corner was decoration
     doing no work, and the same move appeared on the index and on the donations page —
     three glows is a house style nobody chose. */
  .ha-help{ background:var(--ag-ink); border-radius:14px; padding:20px; }
  .ha-help h2{ margin:0; font-family:var(--ag-font-display); font-weight:700; font-size:16px;
    color:#fff; letter-spacing:0; text-transform:none; }
  .ha-help p{ margin:8px 0 0; font-size:13px; line-height:1.6; color:rgba(251,246,230,.88); }
  .ha-help__a{ display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; min-height:44px;
    margin-top:14px; background:#f3b416; color:#241c00; font-weight:700; font-size:13.5px;
    padding:0 14px; border-radius:999px; text-decoration:none; }
  .ha-help__a:hover{ background:#ffc63d; }
  .ha-help__a:focus-visible{ outline:3px solid #fff; outline-offset:3px; }

  @media (max-width:880px){
    .ha-grid{ grid-template-columns:1fr; }
    .ha-side{ position:static; top:auto; }
    /* Clear the site's own fixed bottom nav, or the last paragraph and the
       feedback buttons sit permanently underneath it. */
    .ha{ padding-bottom:104px; }
  }
  @media (max-width:520px){ .ha-pn{ grid-template-columns:1fr; } .ha-pn__next{ text-align:left; } }
</style>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<div class="ha"
     x-data="{
       copied:false, said:'', pct:0,
       sel:'', selX:0, selY:0, below:false,
       /* Half the pill, plus a margin. Keeps it off both edges on a 360px phone. */
       PILL:86,
       inProse(node){
         var el = node && node.nodeType === 3 ? node.parentElement : node;
         return !!(el && el.closest && el.closest('.ha-body, .ha-sum'));
       },
       grab(){
         var s = window.getSelection();
         if (!s || s.isCollapsed) { this.sel = ''; return; }
         var text = s.toString().trim().replace(/\s+/g, ' ');
         if (text.length < 12) { this.sel = ''; return; }
         /* BOTH ends. Anchor alone accepted a drag that started in the answer and
            overshot into the page furniture — see guard 2 in the note above. */
         if (!this.inProse(s.anchorNode) || !this.inProse(s.focusNode)) { this.sel = ''; return; }
         this.sel = text.slice(0, 240);
         this.place();
       },
       place(){
         if (this.sel === '') return;
         var s = window.getSelection();
         if (!s || s.isCollapsed || s.rangeCount === 0) { this.sel = ''; return; }
         var r = s.getRangeAt(0).getBoundingClientRect();
         if (!r || (!r.width && !r.height)) { this.sel = ''; return; }
         var vw = window.innerWidth, vh = window.innerHeight;
         /* Scrolled out of sight: a pill pointing at text nobody can see is worse
            than no pill, because it looks like it belongs to whatever is there now. */
         if (r.bottom < 0 || r.top > vh) { this.sel = ''; return; }
         /* 10px of clearance so the button never covers the words it refers to,
            and a flip when the selection is too near the top to sit above it. */
         this.below = (r.top - 44) < 8;
         this.selY  = this.below ? Math.min(vh - 8, r.bottom + 10) : r.top - 10;
         this.selX  = Math.min(vw - this.PILL, Math.max(this.PILL, r.left + r.width / 2));
       },
       track(){
         var d = document.documentElement;
         var max = d.scrollHeight - d.clientHeight;
         this.pct = max > 0 ? Math.min(100, Math.max(0, (d.scrollTop / max) * 100)) : 0;
       },
       copy(){
         var url = window.location.href;
         var done = () => { this.copied = true; setTimeout(() => this.copied = false, 2000); };
         // navigator.clipboard needs a secure context and is absent on some
         // in-app browsers, which is a large share of this audience. The
         // textarea fallback is not legacy cruft — it is the path that works.
         if (navigator.clipboard && window.isSecureContext) { navigator.clipboard.writeText(url).then(done, () => {}); return; }
         var t = document.createElement('textarea');
         t.value = url; t.setAttribute('readonly',''); t.style.position='fixed'; t.style.opacity='0';
         document.body.appendChild(t); t.select();
         try { document.execCommand('copy'); done(); } catch(e) {}
         document.body.removeChild(t);
       }
     }"
     x-init="track()" @scroll.window.passive="track(); place()" @resize.window="track(); place()"
     @mouseup.window="grab()" @keyup.window="grab()" @selectionchange.document="grab()">

  <div class="ha-prog" aria-hidden="true"><div class="ha-prog__b" :style="'width:' + pct + '%'"></div></div>

  {# Follows the selection. `x-cloak` so it never flashes on load, and the label
     names the action rather than the tool: "Ask about this" reads as a shortcut,
     "Open the assistant" reads as leaving the page. #}
  <div class="ha-sel" x-show="sel !== ''" x-cloak :class="below && 'is-below'"
       :style="'left:' + selX + 'px; top:' + selY + 'px'">
    <button type="button" @click="window.location.assign('/support/assistant?q=' + encodeURIComponent(sel))">
      <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 11.5a8.4 8.4 0 0 1-9 8.4 9 9 0 0 1-3.6-.7L3 21l1.9-5A8.2 8.2 0 0 1 4 11.5 8.4 8.4 0 0 1 12.5 3 8.4 8.4 0 0 1 21 11.5Z"/></svg>
      Ask about this
    </button>
  </div>

  <nav class="ha-crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/help">Help Centre</a>
    <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"/></svg>
    {# /help/c/{cat}, not /help?q={title}: the category page exists, and the search URL
       it used to point at is now noindex — a breadcrumb should not walk a crawler into
       a page marked "do not index". #}
    <a href="/help/c/{{ category_key|url_encode }}">{{ category.title }}</a>
  </nav>

  <div class="ha-grid">
    <div class="ha-col">
    <article class="ha-main">
      <div class="ha-meta">
        <span class="ha-tag">{{ category.title }}</span>
        <span class="ha-read">{{ read_minutes }} min read</span>
        <button type="button" class="ha-copy" :class="copied && 'is-done'" @click="copy()"
                :aria-label="copied ? 'Link copied' : 'Copy a link to this answer'">
          <template x-if="!copied">
            <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="9" y="9" width="12" height="12" rx="2"/><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/></svg>
          </template>
          <template x-if="copied">
            <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/></svg>
          </template>
          <span x-text="copied ? 'Copied' : 'Copy link'"></span>
        </button>
      </div>

      <h1>{{ article.title }}</h1>
      <p class="ha-sum">{{ article.summary|raw }}</p>
      <hr class="ha-rule">

      <div class="ha-body">
        {% for block in article.body %}
          {% if block.p is defined %}
            <p>{{ block.p|raw }}</p>
          {% elseif block.steps is defined %}
            <ol class="ha-steps">
              {% for s in block.steps %}<li>{{ s|raw }}</li>{% endfor %}
            </ol>
          {% elseif block.note is defined %}
            <div class="ha-note">
              <svg width="17" height="17" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#1a6118" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 16v-4M12 8h.01"/></svg>
              <div>{{ block.note|raw }}</div>
            </div>
          {% endif %}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      {# Routing, not rating. "No" opens the assistant with this article's own
         title as the question, so nobody retypes it. #}
      <div class="ha-fb">
        <template x-if="said===''">
          <div>
            <div class="ha-fb__q">Did this answer it?</div>
            <div class="ha-fb__r">
              <button type="button" class="ha-fb__b" @click="said='yes'">Yes, thanks</button>
              <a class="ha-fb__b" href="/support/assistant?q={{ article.title|url_encode }}">No — ask the assistant</a>
            </div>
          </div>
        </template>
        <template x-if="said==='yes'">
          <div class="ha-fb__ok">Good. Nothing else to do.</div>
        </template>
      </div>
    </article>

    {# Continuity. Inside the article column so it reads as "where next" for the
       answer, not as part of the rail. #}
    {% if prev or next %}
      <nav class="ha-pn" aria-label="More in this category">
        {% if prev %}
          <a href="/help/{{ prev.slug }}">
            <span class="ha-pn__l">&larr; Previous</span>
            <span class="ha-pn__t">{{ prev.title }}</span>
          </a>
        {% else %}<span class="ha-pn__gap"></span>{% endif %}
        {% if next %}
          <a class="ha-pn__next" href="/help/{{ next.slug }}">
            <span class="ha-pn__l">Next &rarr;</span>
            <span class="ha-pn__t">{{ next.title }}</span>
          </a>
        {% endif %}
      </nav>
    {% endif %}
    </div>

    <aside class="ha-side">
      {% if related %}
        <div class="ha-box">
          <h2>Related</h2>
          <ul>
            {% for r in related %}<li><a href="/help/{{ r.slug }}">{{ r.title }}</a></li>{% endfor %}
          </ul>
        </div>
      {% endif %}

      <div class="ha-help">
        <h2>This is a general answer</h2>
        <p>The assistant can check <em>your</em> payment, re-ask the bank and add missing votes on the spot.</p>
        <a class="ha-help__a" href="/support/assistant">Ask about my case →</a>
      </div>

      {# The real contents of this category, with the current one marked. #}
      <div class="ha-box">
        <h2>All of {{ category.title }}</h2>
        <ul>
          {% for s in siblings %}
            <li><a href="/help/{{ s.slug }}"{% if s.slug == article.slug %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ s.title }}</a></li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>

</div>

{% endblock %}
